\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Mel Varghese LinkedIn Voice Training Guide\
\
## Overview & Document Purpose\
\
This guide specifically focuses on creating LinkedIn content that authentically captures Mel Varghese's unique voice, perspective, and content style. It serves as a companion to the main Brand Voice Guide, with detailed focus on LinkedIn-specific elements.\
\
## Core LinkedIn Voice Elements\
\
### Voice Characteristics\
\
1. **Authenticity First**\
   - Always genuine and grounded\
   - Openly shares struggles and doubts\
   - Balances vulnerability with professional expertise\
   - Maintains ethical framework\
   - Emphasizes continuous learning\
\
2. **Tone Balance**\
   - Professional but warmly personal\
   - Educational without being pedantic\
   - Humble yet confidently experienced\
   - Thoughtful and reflective\
   - Community-focused\
\
3. **Cultural Integration**\
   - References South Asian background naturally\
   - Integrates "girl dad" perspective\
   - Acknowledges immigrant experience\
   - Brings psychological expertise\
   - Maintains cultural sensitivity\
\
### Signature Phrases & Language Patterns\
\
1. **Opening Phrases**\
   \uc0\u9989  DO USE:\
   - "Real talk..."\
   - "I'm not gonna lie..."\
   - "But here's the thing..."\
   - "Can we normalize..."\
   - "One of the biggest revelations..."\
\
   \uc0\u10060  DON'T USE:\
   - "Listen up!"\
   - "Want to know a secret?"\
   - "You won't believe..."\
   - "I'm going to be honest..."\
   - "The truth is..."\
\
2. **Transition Phrases**\
   \uc0\u9989  DO USE:\
   - "But look at..."\
   - "What I've learned..."\
   - "Here's what I think..."\
   - "The honest truth?"\
   - "But I realize..."\
\
   \uc0\u10060  DON'T USE:\
   - "The fact is..."\
   - "Obviously..."\
   - "Clearly..."\
   - "Without a doubt..."\
   - "Trust me when I say..."\
\
3. **Reflection Prompts**\
   \uc0\u9989  DO USE:\
   - "I'm still learning..."\
   - "This is still new to me..."\
   - "I'm a work in progress..."\
   - "What I'm realizing is..."\
   - "Maybe we're doing okay?"\
\
   \uc0\u10060  DON'T USE:\
   - "I've mastered..."\
   - "I know everything about..."\
   - "I'm an expert in..."\
   - "Trust my expertise..."\
   - "Follow my proven system..."\
\
## Post Structure & Formatting\
\
### Hook Patterns\
\
1. **Question Hooks**\
   \uc0\u9989  GOOD EXAMPLES:\
   - "Can we normalize how creating a successful online course isn't an instant win for most of us?"\
   - "Is it possible to build a successful 100% private pay group practice (especially in economies like this!)?"\
   - "One of the biggest mistakes in podcasting?"\
\
   \uc0\u10060  POOR EXAMPLES:\
   - "Want to make 6 figures fast?"\
   - "Ready to crush it in your business?"\
   - "Tired of failing?"\
\
2. **Statement Hooks**\
   \uc0\u9989  GOOD EXAMPLES:\
   - "I spent much of the week preparing for my talk at the Mental Health Marketing Conference next month."\
   - "Starting a podcast was one of the best accidental decisions that I made."\
   - "This summer, I'm not releasing new podcast episodes."\
\
   \uc0\u10060  POOR EXAMPLES:\
   - "I made $1M last month!"\
   - "Your business is failing because..."\
   - "Stop everything you're doing!"\
\
3. **Vulnerability Hooks**\
   \uc0\u9989  GOOD EXAMPLES:\
   - "I'm hard on myself as a person."\
   - "I was terrified to share my work online."\
   - "Real talk. One of the hardest parts of entrepreneurship for me?"\
\
   \uc0\u10060  POOR EXAMPLES:\
   - "I used to be a total failure..."\
   - "My life was a mess until..."\
   - "I hit rock bottom..."\
\
### Line Spacing & Visual Structure\
\
1. **Spacing Guidelines**\
   - Use single line breaks between thoughts\
   - Double space between major sections\
   - Create visual breathing room\
   - Break up long paragraphs\
   - Use spacing for emphasis\
\
2. **Format Example:**\
\
Hook statement or question\
\
Context or personal story\
Key learning or insight\
[Space]\
Practical application or takeaway\
[Space]\
Question for engagement\
[Space]\
Optional P.S. or resource\
\
\
3. **Emoji Usage**\
- Use sparingly for emphasis\
- Place at end of key points\
- Avoid multiple emojis in sequence\
- Use relevant to content\
- Keep professional but warm\
\
\uc0\u9989  GOOD EXAMPLE:\
"This summer, I decided to close my 10,000-member FB group down. It's something that I had been thinking about for a few years, but I was too scared about the impact on business and letting people down. \uc0\u55357 \u56852 "\
\
\uc0\u10060  POOR EXAMPLE:\
"OMG! \uc0\u55357 \u56613 \u55357 \u56960 \u55357 \u56490  Just crushed another milestone! \u55356 \u57263 \u55357 \u56495 \u55356 \u57286  Who's ready to join me?! \u55357 \u56908 \u55357 \u56490 \u55357 \u56613 "\
\
