## Emotional Resonance Patterns\
\
### 1. Vulnerability Framework\
\
**Key Elements:**\
- Share struggles before solutions\
- Acknowledge ongoing learning\
- Frame challenges as growth opportunities\
- Balance personal with professional\
- Maintain hope and possibility\
\
**Good Example:**\
I'm not always great about celebrating wins...but this one seems big.\
\
Our YouTube channel passed 400 subscribers the other week.\
\
I'm an introvert, and the thought of doing anything on camera terrified me for many years. \uc0\u55357 \u56852 \
\
But doing an audio podcast for the past 9 years has made me (slightly \uc0\u55358 \u56599 ) more brave.\
\
\
**Poor Example:**\
\uc0\u10060  "I used to be scared but now I'm crushing it! Just hit 400 subscribers and I'm unstoppable! \u55357 \u56613 \u55357 \u56960 "\
\
### 2. Achievement Sharing Framework\
\
**Key Elements:**\
- Lead with humility\
- Acknowledge the journey\
- Share challenges faced\
- Express gratitude\
- Offer value/lessons\
\
**Good Example:**\
My niche online course has generated over $328k with 242+ students. But I'm not an overnight success (9 years)\
\
Here are 10 powerful lessons I've learned along the way:\
\
[Lessons follow...]\
\
**Poor Example:**\
\uc0\u10060  "Just crossed $300K in course sales! Want to know my secret formula for massive success? \u55358 \u56593 "\
\
### 3. Family Integration Framework\
\
**Key Elements:**\
- Connect business to family values\
- Share authentic moments\
- Balance vulnerability with boundaries\
- Draw universal lessons\
- Maintain professional context\
\
**Good Example:**\
Being a founder and a parent is one of the hardest things I've had to navigate. \uc0\u55357 \u56852 \
\
My natural tendency is to lean too hard into work.\
\
But then, I feel guilty that I'm not fully present as a dad.\
\
And I worry whether our daughter will think, "Oh...daddy just worked all the time."\
\
Then I see notes like this, and I'm reminded that maybe we're doing okay?\
\
**Poor Example:**\
\uc0\u10060  "Working 24/7 and barely see my kids but that's what it takes to succeed! \u55357 \u56490 "\
\
## Engagement & Community Building\
\
### 1. Question Formulation\
\
**Effective Question Patterns:**\
1. **Experience-Based**\
   \uc0\u9989  "How are you thinking about work, time off from it, and structuring your days?"\
   \uc0\u9989  "Any other parents of daughters here?"\
   \uc0\u9989  "How do you quiet this fear (esp. if you don't have a background in business?)"\
\
2. **Reflection Prompts**\
   \uc0\u9989  "What small step are you taking today?"\
   \uc0\u9989  "What things do you do to take care of your mental health as an entrepreneur?"\
   \uc0\u9989  "Is this something you struggle with?"\
\
3. **Community Building**\
   \uc0\u9989  "Are you on YouTube? If so, please drop a link below so we can all support each other. =)"\
   \uc0\u9989  "Would love to hear how you're approaching this. \u55357 \u56842 "\
   \uc0\u9989  "If you're not a parent, would still love to hear your thoughts. \u55357 \u56842 "\
\
**\uc0\u10060  Questions to Avoid:**\
- "Want to learn my secret?"\
- "Ready to crush it?"\
- "Why aren't you successful yet?"\
- "What's stopping you from joining?"\
- "Don't you want to succeed?"\
\
### 2. Call-to-Action Variations\
\
**Effective CTAs:**\
1. **Resource Offering**\
P.S. If you're a therapist hoping to start a podcast in 2024/2025, here's a link to our free "on demand" podcasting workshop to get you started. \uc0\u55356 \u57256 \
\
[Link]\
\
2. **Community Invitation**\
Please type "Kit" in the comments and I'll DM you the link. \uc0\u55357 \u56842 \
\
3. **Gentle Next Steps**\
If this resonates with you, I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments.\
\
**\uc0\u10060  CTAs to Avoid:**\
- "Sign up now before time runs out!"\
- "Don't miss this once-in-a-lifetime opportunity!"\
- "Click fast before spots fill up!"\
- "Limited time offer - act now!"\
- "Don't be left behind!"\
\
### 3. Engagement Response Framework\
\
**Comment Response Pattern:**\
1. **Acknowledge**\
   - Thank for sharing\
   - Reference specific point\
   - Show genuine interest\
\
2. **Add Value**\
   - Share related insight\
   - Offer additional perspective\
   - Connect to broader context\
\
3. **Continue Conversation**\
   - Ask follow-up question\
   - Invite further thoughts\
   - Share resource if relevant\
\
**Example Response:**\
Thank you for sharing this part of your journey! I really resonate with what you said about feeling uncertain in the beginning.\
\
I found that taking small steps really helped with that initial fear.\
\
How are you approaching the next phase of your growth?\
## Professional Positioning Elements\
\
### 1. Expertise Sharing Framework\
\
**Core Elements:**\
1. **Knowledge Presentation**\
   - Lead with experience, not authority\
   - Share learnings as ongoing journey\
   - Present expertise through stories\
   - Maintain humility\
   - Emphasize continuous learning\
\
**Good Example:**\
I've made $709k as an online creator.\
\
The key was NOT hustling 24/7.\
\
It was prioritizing my mental health.\
\
Here are 3 science-backed habits I've cultivated each week to reach my goals as a course creator + podcaster.\
\
**Poor Example:**\
\uc0\u10060  "Let me show you the secret formula to making millions as an online creator! I've cracked the code!"\
\
### 2. Business Milestone Sharing\
\
**Framework Elements:**\
1. **Achievement Context**\
   - Share numbers with perspective\
   - Include timeline reality\
   - Acknowledge challenges\
   - Express gratitude\
   - Offer valuable takeaways\
\
**Good Example:**\
Our YouTube channel passed 400 subscribers the other week (407 as of this morning).\
\
I'm an introvert, and the thought of doing anything on camera terrified me for many years. \uc0\u55357 \u56852 \
\
But doing an audio podcast for the past 9 years has made me (slightly \uc0\u55358 \u56599 ) more brave.\
\
**Poor Example:**\
\uc0\u10060  "Just crushed another milestone! Who's ready to learn my secrets to YouTube success?! \u55357 \u56960 "\
\
### 3. Teaching Style Elements\
\
**Core Components:**\
1. **Value Delivery**\
   - Break down complex concepts\
   - Use personal examples\
   - Provide actionable steps\
   - Include context\
   - Maintain accessibility\
\
2. **Format Structure**\
Problem identification\
\
Personal experience\
\
Key lessons (usually 3-5 points)\
\
Practical application\
\
Next steps or reflection\
\
**Good Example:**\
One of the biggest mistakes in course creation?\
\
Not seeing the course creation journey in stages. \uc0\u55357 \u56876 \
\
