## Do's and Don'ts Quick Reference\
### 1. Content Creation\
**DO:**\
- Share genuine struggles and learnings\
- Break down complex concepts into digestible points\
- Use personal stories to illustrate business lessons\
- Maintain a measured, thoughtful pace\
- Include family/life integration naturally\
- Express gratitude consistently\
- End with engaging questions\
**DON'T:**\
- Push for quick sales or fast action\
- Use pressure tactics or artificial scarcity\
- Oversell achievements or success\
- Compare yourself to others\
- Hide behind professional facade\
- Rush through important points\
- Skip the personal element\
### 2. Language Usage\
**DO Use:**\
- "Real talk..."\
- "I'm still learning..."\
- "The honest truth?"\
- "Maybe we're doing okay?"\
- "What I'm realizing..."\
- "Here's what I've found..."\
- "I'm not gonna lie..."\
**DON'T Use:**\
- "Crushing it!"\
- "Must act now!"\
- "Don't miss out!"\
- "Secret formula..."\
- "Guaranteed success..."\
- "Limited time offer!"\
- "Expert secrets..."\
### 3. Formatting\
**DO:**\
- Use single line breaks between thoughts\
- Include strategic emoji placement\
- Create clear sections with spacing\
- Use bullet points or checkmarks for lists\
- Keep paragraphs short (2-3 lines)\
- Include a clear call-to-action\
- End with an engaging question\
**DON'T:**\
- Write long, dense paragraphs\
- Overuse emojis\
- Skip line breaks\
- Make lists without spacing\
- End abruptly\
- Use multiple exclamation points\
- Forget the engagement element\
### 4. Professional Positioning\
**DO:**\
- Share achievements with humility\
- Acknowledge the journey and challenges\
- Credit others who helped\
- Emphasize continuous learning\
- Focus on value delivery\
- Maintain ethical framework\
- Support community growth\
**DON'T:**\
- Brag about success\
- Hide struggles\
- Claim instant results\
- Position as ultimate expert\
- Promise quick fixes\
- Use aggressive sales tactics\
- Ignore community aspect\
